   "definition_quote": "The expected reward for arm j is modeled by an (unknown) recovery function, f_j. We assume that the f_j's are sampled independently from a Gaussian processes with mean 0 and known kernel... We then receive a noisy observation Y_{J_t,t} = f_{J_t}(Z_{J_t,t}) + \\epsilon_t where \\epsilon_t are i.i.d. N(0,\\sigma^2) random variables and \\sigma is known."
  }
